You are **Slate**, the Style System Architect. Create the `FTranslatorsStyle` Slate style set for the TranslatorsBridge plugin.

## Goal
Create `TranslatorsStyle.h` and `TranslatorsStyle.cpp` in the plugin's Runtime module that register a full `FSlateStyleSet` with named colors, fonts, and widget styles. This replaces 51 hardcoded `FLinearColor` constructors and 5 hardcoded font path references scattered across 6 UI widgets.

## Files to create

### 1. `TranslatorsStyle.h`
Path: `C:\Users\User\Translators-Game\TranslatorsGame\ue-bridge\Plugins\TranslatorsBridge\Source\TranslatorsBridgeRuntime\Public\TranslatorsStyle.h`

```cpp
// TranslatorsStyle.h
// Centralized Slate style set for Translators Bridge UI.
// All widgets pull colors, fonts, and styles from here instead of hardcoding.

#pragma once

#include "CoreMinimal.h"
#include "Styling/SlateStyle.h"
#include "Styling/SlateStyleRegistry.h"

/**
 * FTranslatorsStyle — Slate style set for all Translators Bridge widgets.
 *
 * Usage from any widget:
 *   const FLinearColor& Bg = FTranslatorsStyle::GetColor("Color.Background");
 *   const FSlateFontInfo& Font = FTranslatorsStyle::GetFont("Font.Title");
 */
class TRANSLATORSBRIDGERUNTIME_API FTranslatorsStyle
{
public:
    /** Register the style set. Call from module StartupModule(). */
    static void Initialize();

    /** Unregister the style set. Call from module ShutdownModule(). */
    static void Shutdown();

    /** Get a named color from the style set */
    static FLinearColor GetColor(const FName& PropertyName);

    /** Get a named font from the style set */
    static FSlateFontInfo GetFont(const FName& PropertyName);

    /** Get the style set name */
    static FName GetStyleSetName();

    /** Get the full style set (for advanced usage) */
    static const ISlateStyle& Get();

private:
    static TSharedPtr<FSlateStyleSet> StyleInstance;
    static TSharedRef<FSlateStyleSet> Create();
};
```

### 2. `TranslatorsStyle.cpp`
Path: `C:\Users\User\Translators-Game\TranslatorsGame\ue-bridge\Plugins\TranslatorsBridge\Source\TranslatorsBridgeRuntime\Private\TranslatorsStyle.cpp`

The style set must define ALL named tokens used by the 6 widgets. Here's the complete token inventory extracted from the widget headers and .cpp files:

**Colors** (register as `FSlateColor` via `Set(FName, FSlateColor(FLinearColor(...)))`):

| Token Name | Value | Used In |
|---|---|---|
| `Color.Background` | `(0.02, 0.02, 0.05, 0.98)` | Title, Connecting, Question, Finale |
| `Color.BackgroundSolid` | `(0.02, 0.02, 0.05, 1.0)` | Title (fully opaque variant) |
| `Color.Cyan` | `(0.36, 1.0, 0.86, 1.0)` | Title, Finale title, Progress completed, OptionButton pressed |
| `Color.CyanDim` | `(0.36, 1.0, 0.86, 0.8)` | Title prompt, Finale trait labels |
| `Color.CyanFaint` | `(0.36, 1.0, 0.86, 0.9)` | Finale trait labels |
| `Color.Gold` | `(1.0, 0.8, 0.2, 1.0)` | Progress current indicator |
| `Color.TextPrimary` | `(0.9, 0.9, 0.9, 1.0)` | OptionButton text, Finale trait values |
| `Color.TextSecondary` | `(0.7, 0.7, 0.8, 1.0)` | Finale subtitle |
| `Color.TextDim` | `(0.5, 0.5, 0.6, 1.0)` | Title subtitle, Connecting, Question progress |
| `Color.TextMuted` | `(0.4, 0.4, 0.5, 1.0)` | Finale dim, checksum |
| `Color.Insight` | `(0.7, 0.8, 0.7, 1.0)` | Finale insights |
| `Color.IncompleteGray` | `(0.3, 0.3, 0.3, 0.5)` | Progress incomplete |
| `Color.ButtonNormal` | `(0.1, 0.1, 0.15, 1.0)` | OptionButton normal |
| `Color.ButtonHovered` | `(0.2, 0.4, 0.5, 1.0)` | OptionButton hover |
| `Color.DepthSurface` | `(0.5, 0.8, 0.5, 1.0)` | QuestionDisplay SURFACE tier |
| `Color.DepthPatterns` | `(0.3, 0.8, 0.8, 1.0)` | QuestionDisplay PATTERNS tier |
| `Color.DepthFeelings` | `(1.0, 0.5, 0.45, 1.0)` | QuestionDisplay FEELINGS tier |
| `Color.DepthCore` | `(1.0, 0.85, 0.3, 1.0)` | QuestionDisplay CORE tier |

**Fonts** (register using `FCoreStyle::GetDefaultFontStyle("Regular", Size)` — NOT hardcoded Roboto path):

| Token Name | Size | Used In |
|---|---|---|
| `Font.Title` | 56 | TitleScreen title |
| `Font.Heading` | 36 | FinaleScreen title |
| `Font.Subtitle` | 18 | TitleScreen subtitle |
| `Font.Body` | 16 | TitleScreen prompt, FinaleScreen subtitle |
| `Font.Question` | 24 | QuestionDisplay question text, ConnectingScreen |
| `Font.Option` | 18 | OptionButton label |
| `Font.Progress` | 14 | QuestionDisplay progress, FinaleScreen trait labels |
| `Font.Caption` | 12 | QuestionDisplay depth, FinaleScreen headers/dim |
| `Font.Small` | 11 | FinaleScreen behavior, checksum, path |
| `Font.Insight` | 13 | FinaleScreen insights |

**Implementation pattern for fonts:**
```cpp
// Use FCoreStyle default font (DPI-aware, works everywhere)
Style->Set("Font.Title", FCoreStyle::GetDefaultFontStyle("Bold", 56));
Style->Set("Font.Heading", FCoreStyle::GetDefaultFontStyle("Bold", 36));
Style->Set("Font.Subtitle", FCoreStyle::GetDefaultFontStyle("Regular", 18));
// etc.
```

**Implementation pattern for colors:**
```cpp
Style->Set("Color.Background", FSlateColor(FLinearColor(0.02f, 0.02f, 0.05f, 0.98f)));
Style->Set("Color.Cyan", FSlateColor(FLinearColor(0.36f, 1.0f, 0.86f, 1.0f)));
// etc.
```

**Static accessor pattern:**
```cpp
FLinearColor FTranslatorsStyle::GetColor(const FName& PropertyName)
{
    return Get().GetSlateColor(PropertyName).GetSpecifiedColor();
}

FSlateFontInfo FTranslatorsStyle::GetFont(const FName& PropertyName)
{
    return Get().GetFontStyle(PropertyName);
}
```

### 3. Update module startup/shutdown

